            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/estoraged.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rom Lemarchand",
                        "email": "romlem@google.com",
                        "username": "romlem-goog"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we pass -y as well? \n\nSee: https://linux.die.net/man/8/fsck"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/estoraged.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Wedig",
                        "email": "johnwedig@google.com",
                        "username": "johnwedig"
                    },
                    "message": "For ext4, it looks like you can't pass in -p and -y together, according to this documentation: https://linux.die.net/man/8/e2fsck\n\nI tried it on a machine, and got this error:\n\n```\n$ fsck -t ext4 -p /dev/mapper/luks-mmcblk0 -y\nfsck from util-linux 2.39.3\ne2fsck: Only one of the options -p/-a, -n or -y may be specified.\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/estoraged.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Wedig",
                        "email": "johnwedig@google.com",
                        "username": "johnwedig"
                    },
                    "message": "I guess we could just use -y option by itself and not use -p. The documentation seems to imply that this might do some \"unsafe\" fixes, which may or may not be a concern for us."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/estoraged.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rom Lemarchand",
                        "email": "romlem@google.com",
                        "username": "romlem-goog"
                    },
                    "message": "I think -p is the right option here as if there are issues, we will likely just offer to wipe the whole eMMC anyway."
                }
            ],
